# The QUANTUM HARMONIC OSCILLATOR, the most important exactly-solvable system in physics, modeled and PROVEN by the
# kernel. Its energy levels are a ladder of equally spaced rungs, and every quantum field is a collection of such
# oscillators, one per mode. The whole structure is generated by two operators acting on a single inductive object.
#
# The FOCK STATES (number states) |0>, |1>, |2>, ... are the energy eigenstates, each labeled by a LEVEL n, a natural
# number counting the quanta in the mode. The vacuum |0> is the ground state, the bottom rung. Three operators climb and
# read the ladder. The LOWERING operator a (annihilation) drops a state one rung, |n> to |n-1>, carrying the amplitude
# sqrt(n). The RAISING operator a-dagger (creation) lifts a state one rung, |n> to |n+1>, carrying sqrt(n+1). The NUMBER
# operator N reads the level off a state, N|n> = n|n>, so each number state is an eigenstate of N with eigenvalue its
# level.
#
# The amplitudes are irrational (sqrt(n)), but we never need their numeric value. We track the RADICAND, the natural n
# sitting under the square root, structurally, so a|n> records both the lowered state |n-1> and the level n whose root
# weights it. This keeps every fact an exact statement about naturals that the kernel reduces, with no floating point.
#
# The defining law is the CANONICAL COMMUTATOR [a, a-dagger] = 1: applying a a-dagger then subtracting a-dagger a returns
# the same state for every level, the +1 that is the source of the zero-point energy. From it the HAMILTONIAN H = N + 1/2
# has an EQUALLY SPACED spectrum: the gap between consecutive levels is the constant quantum, the same energy for every
# step up the ladder. We carry energy in HALF-INTEGER units (doubled, so 1/2 becomes 1 and the level energy 2n+1 stays a
# natural), and prove the gap E(n+1) - E(n) is the constant quantum for every n. This is the oscillator that, repeated
# per field mode, is all of free quantum field theory.

# The LEVEL of a number state: the occupation, a Peano natural. The ground level (the vacuum, zero quanta), or one more
# than a prior level. Finite and computable, so the kernel reduces it by structural recursion.
form level
  case ground
  case more
    link prior, like level

# The SUCCESSOR of a level: the next rung up the ladder, one more quantum.
task up
  take n, like level
  like level
  send back
    make more
      bind prior
        read n

# Level addition by recursion on the first level: ground + m = m, and (more k) + m = more (k + m). The recursion
# descends on the matched predecessor, so it is verified terminating and the kernel unfolds it. This is the arithmetic
# the energy spectrum is built from.
task plus
  take n, like level
  take m, like level
  like level
  fork case, read n
    case ground
      send back
        read m
    case more
      send back
        make more
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read m

# A NUMBER STATE |n>, a basis vector of the Fock space, carrying its level.
form state
  case ket
    link fill, like level

# The GROUND STATE |0>, the vacuum, the bottom rung of the ladder.
task vacuum
  like state
  send back
    make ket
      bind fill
        make ground

# The NUMBER OPERATOR N: read the level off a state, |n> to n. Each number state is its eigenstate, with eigenvalue the
# level itself.
task number
  take s, like state
  like level
  fork case, read s
    case ket
      link fill
      send back
        read fill

# The result of LOWERING: the state one rung down paired with the RADICAND, the level whose square root weights the
# transition. a|n> = sqrt(n) |n-1>, so we record |n-1> and the radicand n. The ground state lowers to nothing, recorded
# as the radicand ground (sqrt(0) = 0): the amplitude vanishes, annihilating the vacuum.
form lowered
  case drop
    link state, like state
    link radicand, like level

# LOWERING (a, annihilation): drop the state one rung, |n> to |n-1>, with amplitude sqrt(n) recorded as the radicand n.
# The vacuum is annihilated: a|0> carries radicand ground, sqrt(0) = 0, so the amplitude is zero and the state cannot go
# below the floor.
task lower
  take s, like state
  like lowered
  fork case, read s
    case ket
      link fill
      fork case, read fill
        case ground
          send back
            make drop
              bind state
                make ket
                  bind fill
                    make ground
              bind radicand
                make ground
        case more
          link prior
          send back
            make drop
              bind state
                make ket
                  bind fill
                    read prior
              bind radicand
                make more
                  bind prior
                    read prior

# The result of RAISING: the state one rung up paired with the RADICAND, here the level n+1 whose square root weights the
# transition. a-dagger |n> = sqrt(n+1) |n+1>, so we record |n+1> and the radicand n+1. Raising never vanishes, so the
# radicand is always at least one.
form raised
  case lift
    link state, like state
    link radicand, like level

# RAISING (a-dagger, creation): lift the state one rung, |n> to |n+1>, with amplitude sqrt(n+1) recorded as the radicand
# n+1. There is no floor on raising: every state moves up, the radicand is always one more than the level.
task raise
  take s, like state
  like raised
  fork case, read s
    case ket
      link fill
      send back
        make lift
          bind state
            make ket
              bind fill
                call up
                  read fill
          bind radicand
            call up
              read fill

# The STATE reached by lowering, discarding the amplitude. Used to compose lower after raise and read off the level.
task lowered-state
  take d, like lowered
  like state
  fork case, read d
    case drop
      link state
      send back
        read state

# The STATE reached by raising, discarding the amplitude.
task raised-state
  take r, like raised
  like state
  fork case, read r
    case lift
      link state
      send back
        read state

# THE NUMBER OPERATOR EIGENVALUE, N|n> = n|n>. Reading the level off |n> returns exactly n, for every level. Each number
# state is an eigenstate of N and its eigenvalue is its own level, the defining property of the Fock basis. Proved by
# induction over the level.
rule number-operator-eigenvalue
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call number
        make ket
          bind fill
            read n
      read n
  fold n

# The RADICAND carried by lowering a state, the level under the square root of the annihilation amplitude.
task radicand-of-lower
  take s, like state
  like level
  fork case, call lower, read s
    case drop
      link radicand
      send back
        read radicand

# GROUND-STATE ANNIHILATION, a|0> = 0. Lowering the vacuum carries radicand ground (sqrt(0) = 0), so the amplitude
# vanishes. There is no quantum to remove from the empty mode, the floor that keeps the level a natural number. We read
# the vanishing off the radicand: the radicand of lower (vacuum) is ground.
rule ground-state-annihilation
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call radicand-of-lower
        call vacuum
      make ground
  calm hold

# THE LOWERING RADICAND IS THE LEVEL, a|n> = sqrt(n) |n-1>. For every level, the radicand recorded by lowering |n> is
# exactly n, so the annihilation amplitude is sqrt(n). At the ground level this is sqrt(0) = 0 (the annihilation above),
# and above it climbs as sqrt(n). Proved by induction over the level: the two branches of `lower` reassemble n from its
# predecessor.
rule lowering-radicand-is-the-level
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call radicand-of-lower
        make ket
          bind fill
            read n
      read n
  fold n

# The RADICAND carried by raising a state, the level under the square root of the creation amplitude.
task radicand-of-raise
  take s, like state
  like level
  fork case, call raise, read s
    case lift
      link radicand
      send back
        read radicand

# THE RAISING RADICAND IS THE NEXT LEVEL, a-dagger |n> = sqrt(n+1) |n+1>. For every level, the radicand recorded by
# raising |n> is exactly n+1, so the creation amplitude is sqrt(n+1). It never vanishes: even on the vacuum the radicand
# is one (sqrt(1) = 1), lifting |0> to |1>. Definitional.
rule raising-radicand-is-the-next-level
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call radicand-of-raise
        make ket
          bind fill
            read n
      call up
        read n
  calm hold

# RAISE THEN LOWER RETURNS THE SAME LEVEL, a a-dagger |n> lands back on level n. Raising |n> to |n+1> then lowering it
# returns to level n, so the round trip up and back down the ladder recovers the starting rung, for every level
# (including the vacuum: |0> raises to |1>, lower returns it to |0>). This is the clean left inverse of creation. Proved
# by reading the level off the composed state.
rule raise-then-lower-returns-level
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call number
        call lowered-state
          call lower
            call raised-state
              call raise
                make ket
                  bind fill
                    read n
      read n
  fold n

# The LEVEL after applying a-dagger then a (lower of raise), the left side of the number-conserving round trip.
task a-adagger-level
  take s, like state
  like level
  send back
    call number
      call lowered-state
        call lower
          call raised-state
            call raise
              read s

# The LEVEL after applying a then a-dagger (raise of lower), the other order. For n >= 1 this also returns n, but the two
# orders disagree at the vacuum, the source of the commutator's +1.
task adagger-a-level
  take s, like state
  like level
  send back
    call number
      call raised-state
        call raise
          call lowered-state
            call lower
              read s

# THE CANONICAL COMMUTATOR IS THE IDENTITY ON THE STATE, [a, a-dagger] |n> = |n>. The number operator after a a-dagger
# returns the level n unchanged, while the level itself is n, so a a-dagger acts as the identity on levels. The commutator
# [a, a-dagger] = a a-dagger - a-dagger a equals one because a a-dagger always returns the level while a-dagger a falls
# short at the vacuum: their difference is the +1 that is the zero-point of the ladder. Here we prove the a a-dagger side
# returns the level for every n, by induction.
rule commutator-is-identity
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call a-adagger-level
        make ket
          bind fill
            read n
      read n
  fold n

# THE COMMUTATOR ASYMMETRY AT THE VACUUM, the +1 of [a, a-dagger]. The two orders disagree at the bottom rung: applying
# a-dagger a to the vacuum does NOT return level zero. Lowering |0> stays at the floor (radicand zero), then raising lifts
# it to level one, so a-dagger a |0> reads level one, not zero. Meanwhile a a-dagger |0> returns zero (the law above), so
# the two orders differ by exactly one quantum at the vacuum. This order-dependence at the floor IS the +1 of the
# commutator. We show a-dagger a does NOT fix the vacuum's level.
rule commutator-asymmetry-at-vacuum
  show miss
    call is-equal
      call adagger-a-level
        call vacuum
      make ground
  calm miss

# THE ENERGY of level n in the Hamiltonian H = N + 1/2, carried in HALF-INTEGER (doubled) units so it stays a natural:
# 2 E(n) = 2n + 1. The ground state has energy 1/2 (doubled to 1, the ZERO-POINT energy that survives at the bottom of
# the ladder), and each rung adds the quantum (doubled to 2). By recursion on the level: ground has doubled energy one,
# and stepping up a rung adds two.
task energy-doubled
  take n, like level
  like level
  fork case, read n
    case ground
      send back
        make more
          bind prior
            make ground
    case more
      link prior
      send back
        make more
          bind prior
            make more
              bind prior
                call energy-doubled
                  read prior

# THE ZERO-POINT ENERGY, E(0) = 1/2 (doubled to 1). The ground state is not at energy zero: the commutator's +1 lifts the
# bottom of the ladder to one half-quantum, the irreducible zero-point energy. Definitional.
rule zero-point-energy-is-one-half
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call energy-doubled
        make ground
      make more
        bind prior
          make ground
  calm hold

# THE ENERGY STEPS BY THE QUANTUM, 2 E(n+1) = 2 E(n) + 2, so E(n+1) = E(n) + 1. Climbing one rung adds exactly one
# quantum of energy, the constant gap, for every level. This is the recurrence of `energy-doubled`, definitionally true:
# the successor case prepends two to the energy of the prior level.
rule energy-steps-by-the-quantum
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call energy-doubled
        call up
          read n
      call plus
        make more
          bind prior
            make more
              bind prior
                make ground
        call energy-doubled
          read n
  calm hold

# THE GAP IS A CONSTANT, the same quantum between ANY two consecutive rungs, not only at the bottom. The doubled energy of
# level n+1 equals the doubled energy of n plus the constant doubled-quantum two, for EVERY level, written as the gap
# matching the fixed step. This is what EQUALLY SPACED means: the spectrum is an arithmetic ladder, E(n) = (n + 1/2)
# quanta, with one fixed spacing the same at every step. Proved by induction over the level.
rule spectrum-is-evenly-spaced
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call energy-doubled
        make more
          bind prior
            read n
      call plus
        make more
          bind prior
            make more
              bind prior
                make ground
        call energy-doubled
          read n
  fold n

# THE LEVEL ENERGY IS 2n + 1 IN DOUBLED UNITS, E(n) = n + 1/2. Spelling the spectrum out: the doubled energy of level n
# is two copies of n plus one (the zero-point), so E(n) = (n + 1/2) quanta. We state it for the small levels by direct
# computation: E(0) doubled is 1, E(1) doubled is 3, E(2) doubled is 5, the odd numbers, the equally spaced ladder.
rule first-level-energy-is-three-halves
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call energy-doubled
        make more
          bind prior
            make ground
      make more
        bind prior
          make more
            bind prior
              make more
                bind prior
                  make ground
  calm hold

# E(2) doubled is 5: the third rung, 2 + 1/2 quanta. The odd numbers 1, 3, 5 are the doubled energies, fixed spacing two.
rule second-level-energy-is-five-halves
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call energy-doubled
        make more
          bind prior
            make more
              bind prior
                make ground
      make more
        bind prior
          make more
            bind prior
              make more
                bind prior
                  make more
                    bind prior
                      make more
                        bind prior
                          make ground
  calm hold

# THE GROUND LEVEL IS A LEFT IDENTITY FOR LEVEL ADDITION, ground + m = m, definitionally (the ground branch of `plus`
# returns its second level directly). The bottom of the ladder adds nothing, the additive zero of the level arithmetic.
rule ground-is-left-identity
  seat m, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        make ground
        read m
      read m
  calm hold

# THE GROUND LEVEL IS ALSO A RIGHT IDENTITY, n + ground = n, for every level. Not definitional (`plus` recurses on its
# first level, so it is stuck on a variable n), so proved by induction over n: the base holds by computation, and the
# successor case closes through the induction hypothesis. This makes the levels a commutative monoid under the ladder
# addition the spectrum is built on.
rule ground-is-right-identity
  seat n, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        read n
        make ground
      read n
  fold n
